 "_provenance": "γ = −mean(SantaLucia 1998 unified NN stacking ΔG37) over human proximal promoter TSS−2000..+500 (2501 bp); db=nuccore efetch by accession+1-based window+strand; assembly GRCh38 (current RefSeq chromosomes). MEASURED [V], never fitted.",
 "_level_vs_shape": "DNA v1.13: γ and A4 are the LEVEL and SHAPE of one stiffness field — orthogonal projections, neither contains the other (A4 = signal − γ; |mean(shape)|=0 by construction). Reading γ ALONE is the compressed view; this atlas carries both.",
 "_olfaction_note": "OLFACTION BREAKS THE WAVE SKELETON. Vision/hearing: a WAVE property → a single PHYSICAL place (angle/membrane position) → one R19 switch. Smell: the stimulus is a MOLECULE — no wave, no single place — so the identity code is COMBINATORIAL across the OR repertoire (a pattern over many R19 switches). γ reads each gene's promoter switch-THRESHOLD structure (the expression/excitability layer); it does NOT encode odorant→receptor LIGAND specificity, which lives in the receptor protein's binding pocket (coding sequence + 3D structure) and is the named [O]. The surviving universal is the R19 transduction switch (the olfactory CNG channel).",
